  "summary": "Otome ( 乙女 ) is a Japanese fashion and lifestyle that emerged in the late 1970s.",
  "description": "Otome ( 乙女 ) is a Japanese fashion and lifestyle that emerged in the late 1970s. It is characterized by casual, feminine clothing with youthful, vintage-inspired visuals and an emphasis on traditional handicrafts and hobbies. The style is widely regarded as one of the predecessors of Lolita fashion. While the term \"otome\" was once solely used as name for the aesthetic in Japan, its meaning later shifted due to an increasing association with female-oriented otaku culture, diluting the association with fashion.",
